<h1>Zoe Ma</h1>
<p>Affordable housing developer. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Builds and manages affordable apartment buildings, chairs the Cook County Green Party, and says she would be the city&#39;s first Chinese American, Muslim, and naturalized mayor; grew up working-class in China and arrived in Chicago in 1994 with $40. Filed 17,000 signatures.</p>
<p><a href="https://zoemaformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (zoemaformayor.com)</a></p>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Friends of Zoe Ma for Mayor</li>
<li>Raised: $60K</li>
<li>Spent: $65K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $3,228</li>
<li>Since the committee formed May 28, 2026, through Sept. 30. Nearly all of it was loans from one Wilmette company. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41198" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 0.0 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>What they would do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Guaranteed income as a top priority, pointing to the city&#39;s pilot that helped people keep their homes. <q>Chicago&#39;s never short on money. It&#39;s about priority.</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Sept. 1, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Follow the money to see how much actually reaches affordable housing. <q>Let&#39;s follow the money</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Sept. 1, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Opportunity for everyone in the city: property tax reform, youth poverty, and free career tutoring in the public schools. <q>I think that opportunity should be available to everyone in the city</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Sept. 1, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>Main points</h3>
<p>Poverty: A guaranteed income program as the first priority, costed at about $6 million for 1,000 people for a year.</p>
<p>Housing money: Audit where the affordable housing money goes, from a developer who builds it.</p>
<p>Also: Property tax reform, youth poverty, and free career tutoring in the public schools.</p>
<h3>Next to the others</h3>
<p>Only Ma: Guaranteed income as the lead issue.</p>
<p>Housing: Ma builds affordable housing; Brewer ran the housing authority; Giannoulias, Quigley, and Holberg set unit targets.</p>
<p>Money: Ma says the city is never short of money, only of priorities; Quinlan and Kitover say it is near collapse.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Says the city has the money and lacks only the priorities; would trace where the affordable housing money goes and fund guaranteed income at a few million dollars a year.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>Even if we find like 1,000 people for guaranteed income for a year, that&#39;s only $6 million</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Sept. 1, 2026</a>)</li>
<li><q>Let&#39;s see how much money actually goes toward affordable housing, while we have $425 million could really help.</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Sept. 1, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Says she joined the 1989 Tiananmen Square protests before coming to Chicago with $40. (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-mayoral-candidate-zoe-ma-poverty-inequality/" rel="nofollow noopener">cbsnews.com</a>)</li>
